%SIXMD 1
# @?WHICH - LOCATE AN EXTERNAL COMMAND

## @?OPERANDS

### @?COMMAND...
ONE OR MORE COMMAND NAMES OR EXPLICIT PATHS.

## DESCRIPTION

WHICH SEARCHES THE NATIVE EXECUTABLE PATH USED FOR INSTALLED SYSTEM COMMANDS
AND PRINTS THE PUBLIC EXEC PATH FOR EACH COMMAND FOUND.  SYSTEM COMMANDS
PRECEDE OPTION/BASE COMMANDS.  AN OPERAND CONTAINING / IS TESTED AS AN
EXPLICIT PATH.

PUBLIC COMMANDS IMPLEMENTED BY SHARED MULTIPLEXERS ARE REPORTED UNDER
/SYSTEM/EXEC; THEIR PRIVATE IMPLEMENTATIONS REMAIN IN /SYSTEM/LIBEXEC.

WHICH LOCATES EXTERNAL COMMANDS.  DSH BUILTINS, FUNCTIONS, AND ALIASES ARE
SHELL STATE AND ARE NOT REPORTED BY THIS UTILITY.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - ALL COMMANDS WERE FOUND
### @?1 - ONE OR MORE COMMANDS WERE NOT FOUND OR OUTPUT FAILED
### @?2 - INVALID USAGE
